        "Alexandre Blais",
        "Andreas Wallraff",
        "Robert J. Schoelkopf"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Circuit QED made the interaction of individual artificial atoms and microwave photons a precise, controllable experimental regime, with lasting foundational and technological impact.",
        "attribution": "Blais supplied a decisive theoretical framework, while Wallraff and Schoelkopf established the experimental architecture; Girvin's foundational theoretical role also deserves careful consideration.",
        "maturity": "The phenomena and platform have been independently reproduced, elaborated, and made central to quantum optics and superconducting quantum technology.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The boundary between this achievement and already recognized superconducting-circuit breakthroughs requires careful delineation."
        ]
      }
    },
